From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: windows.applicationmodel: implement PackageCatalog, with weak references

winget's installed-packages source opens Windows.ApplicationModel.
PackageCatalog for the current user to follow MSIX installs, so `winget list`
and every install failed at "Failed to open the predefined source" with
REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG.

Add the class (IPackageCatalogStatics: OpenForCurrentUser;
OpenForCurrentPackage fails with APPMODEL_ERROR_NO_PACKAGE outside a package)
and IPackageCatalog's five events, which can be subscribed and removed. Nothing
raises them yet, since nothing deploys MSIX packages yet.

C++/WinRT registers such handlers with auto-revoke, which takes a weak
reference to the event source; without IWeakReferenceSource winget
dereferenced null. The catalog gives real weak references: Resolve returns
the object while it has strong references -- taking one with a compare-and-
swap that never revives a dying object -- and null once it is gone.

Declares IPackageCatalog, its statics, event arguments and handlers in
windows.applicationmodel.idl, and GetCurrentPackageFullName/FamilyName in
appmodel.h, where they were missing.

